l thoughts before public response\" and a suggested public response. We need to output our own public message. Since we are Agent 3, we need to respond to Agent 2's contribution. Agent 2 recommended Candidate D, with strengths and concerns. We need to either agree, challenge, or add. According to guidelines, we should make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing the discussion, using explicit facts, and state our vote.\n\nWe have our own notes: same as Agent 2's. We can either agree with D, or propose another candidate. Let's consider: maybe Candidate C has strong anticipation of dangerous situations, leadership, spatial vision, but concerns about being unfriendly and unhealthy eating. The unhealthy eating is not a safety-critical factor. Unfriendly is a crew cooperation issue. Candidate B is conscientious, handles stress, good weather assessment, but has wrong tone and pretentious. Candidate A quick decisions, attention, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nWhich is best? D has hot temper and know-it-all, which could be serious. B's nasty remarks also serious. A's egocentric and communication difficulty also serious. C's unfriendly and show-off also serious. All have cooperation concerns. Which is least? Hard to decide. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate C's leadership and ability to anticipate dangerous situations is crucial for long-distance flights, and his technical abilities (spatial vision, complex connections) outweigh his unfriendly demeanor, which could be mitigated with training. Also his leadership could improve crew cooperation. So we could propose Candidate C as alternative.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 2's points. We can say: I see the strengths of D, but I am concerned about hot temper and know-it-all, which could impair crew cooperation more than C's unfriendly but strong leadership. Provide evidence: C can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concern: C is unfriendly. Compare: D's hot temper may cause immediate conflict, while C's unfriendly may be less disruptive. Also D's \"responds to unexpected events adequately\" vs C's anticipation of dangerous situations (proactive). So I might shift my vote to C.\n\nThus my public message: I appreciate Agent 2's points, but I think Candidate C offers stronger safety-critical competencies (anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, leadership) and his cooperation concerns are less severe. So I propose Candidate C as my provisional recommendation.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: \"anticipates dangerous situations\", \"very good leadership qualities\", \"unfriendly\". Also mention D's hot temper and know-it-all.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
